From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Venus Build Fix <noreply@example.com>
Date: Sat, 22 Aug 2026 00:00:00 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] Kconfig.venus: select the remaining container-required
 cgroup v2 controllers

The VENUS symbol's cgroups selects on this branch only cover CGROUPS,
CGROUP_CPUACCT, CGROUP_SCHED and the tailscale-related NET_SCHED group -
nothing for cpuset, memory, io or pids. This board's own defconfig
already sets these explicitly, so this is a no-op here, but Kconfig.venus
should still be the authoritative source so all container-capable
machines are configured the same way rather than relying on per-board
defconfig defaults that don't exist everywhere (einstein, am62xx).

Upstream-Status: Inappropriate [Venus specific]

---
 Kconfig.venus | 4 ++++
 1 file changed, 4 insertions(+)

--- a/Kconfig.venus
+++ b/Kconfig.venus
@@ -41,6 +41,10 @@
 	select CGROUPS
 	select CGROUP_CPUACCT
 	select CGROUP_SCHED
+	select CPUSETS
+	select MEMCG
+	select BLK_CGROUP
+	select CGROUP_PIDS
 	select NET_SCHED
 	select NET_CLS_ACT
 	select NET_SCH_HTB
--
2.43.0
